<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="letter-spacing: -0.1pt">These consolidated financial statements
have been prepared using the historical cost convention except for financial instruments which have been measured at fair value. These
consolidated financial statements were prepared on an accrual basis except for cash flow information.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt"><FONT STYLE="letter-spacing: -0.1pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="letter-spacing: -0.1pt">These consolidated financial statements
incorporate the financial statements of the Company and its 100% owned subsidiary. The accounts of the Company&rsquo;s subsidiary are
prepared for the same reporting period as the parent company, using consistent accounting policies. Inter-company transactions, balances
and unrealized gains or losses on transactions are eliminated. The Company&rsquo;s subsidiary is the following:</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

