<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 0 14.2pt; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">The risk-free interest rate is the yield on zero-coupon Canadian
Treasury Bills of a term consistent with the assumed option life. The expected life of the option is the average expected period to exercise.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 0 14.2pt; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 0 14.2pt; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">Volatility is based on the available historical volatility of the
Company&rsquo;s share price, excluding specific time frames in which volatility was affected by specific transactions that are not considered
to be indicative of the Company&rsquo;s expected share price volatility. The Company has not declared dividends in the past.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 0 14.2pt; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

