<TD STYLE="text-align: right; width: 0%"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 20pt"><B>15.</B></TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="letter-spacing: -0.1pt"><B>Financial
                                            instruments and risk management (continued)</B></FONT></TD>
</TR>
</TABLE>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">The Company thoroughly examines the various financial instruments and risks
to which it is exposed and assesses the impact and likelihood of those risks. These risks include foreign currency risk, interest rate
risk, market risk, credit risk, and liquidity risk. Where material, these risks are reviewed and monitored by the Board of Directors</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">There have been no changes in any risk management policies since December 31,
2024.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="width: 100%; font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">
<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: justify">
<TD STYLE="text-align: right; width: 0%"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 20pt"><B>16.</B></TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify"><B>Capital management</B></TD>
</TR>
</TABLE></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">The Company defines capital that it manages as shareholders&rsquo; equity.
The Company manages its capital structure in order to have funds available to support its research and development and sustain the future
development of the business. When managing capital, the Company&rsquo;s objective is to ensure the entity continues as a going concern
as well as to maintain optimal returns to shareholders and benefits for other stakeholders. Management adjusts the capital structure as
necessary in order to support its activities.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">Since inception, the Company&rsquo;s objective in managing capital is to ensure
sufficient liquidity to finance its research and development activities, general and administrative expenses, expenses associated with
intellectual property protection, and its overall capital expenditures. There were no changes during the year ended December 31, 2025.
The Company is not exposed to external requirements by regulatory agencies regarding its capital.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 10pt; font-size: 10pt"></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 10pt; font-size: 10pt"><FONT STYLE="letter-spacing: -0.1pt"><TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="width: 100%; font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">
